WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Three areas, an 84-second accessible tour. This is a conceptual action script, not a confirmed site, roster or implementation authorisation.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:24.000
06:00–10:00 | Zhongzhiyuan Maintenance Yard: technicians arrive through a staffed entrance for questions, equipment explanation and handover. AI only assists explanation and lookup. Pause if staffed access, no-scan service or a continuous accessible route is missing.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:42.000
10:00–18:00 | AI Origin Handover Yard: learners, caregivers and low-digital-literacy users reach learning, rest and service desks through visual, tactile and staffed wayfinding. AI never replaces care judgement or infers identity or emotion.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:01:00.000
18:00–24:00 | Dazhongsi Exchange Yard: couriers, small-shop operators and night workers move safely among transfer, short rest, supplies, handover and help. Cash and staffed counters remain available; scanning is never a condition of service.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:18.000
00:00–06:00 | Recovery and safe departure: the three yards support night recovery through lighting, rest, staffed handover and clear exits. Do not continue opening when routes are blocked, staff are absent or accessibility is interrupted.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Shared boundary: AI only assists. Keep staffed access, no-scan service and a continuous accessible route. Pause and independently review on covert tracking, personal scoring, automated punishment or production-system connection.
